  "servings": 6,
  "summary": "Celebrate the conclusion of your meal with this luscious <b>Mexican roasted pumpkin dessert</b> infused with warm aromatic spices and sweet caramel notes. Thick wedges of heirloom <b>calabaza pumpkin</b> are coated in a glaze of melted butter, unrefined <b>piloncillo sugar</b>, wild honey, and aromatic orange zest before baking. As the pumpkin roasts in a hot oven, its natural sugars caramelize alongside cinnamon sticks, star anise, and fragrant ground cloves to create a deeply fragrant crust. The flesh becomes silky smooth while holding its graceful shape, offering a delightful contrast between charred spiced edges and sweet tender interior. Drizzled generously with creamy goat milk <b>cajeta caramel</b> and sprinkled with crunchy toasted pepitas, this dessert showcases traditional Mexican baking artistry. Serve warm with vanilla ice cream or fresh whipped cream for an unforgettable sweet course that honors rustic seasonal flavors in every bite.",
